<title>UK: Halifax no immediate plans to change rates.</title>
<headline>Halifax no immediate plans to change rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's biggest mortgage lender Halifax Building Society said on Wednesday it would make no immediate change to its mortgage rate following the Bank of England's decision to raise interest rates.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the building society said Halifax would keep its rates under review but planned no immediate adjustment.  </p>
<p>Halifax's current standard variable mortgage rate is 6.99 percent, which was introduced for existing borrowers on August 1.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
